# Files the openapi-generator-maven-plugin must NOT write into
# service/target/generated-sources/openapi.
#
# The spring generator emits a full sample application next to the API interfaces; that sample
# would collide with the real Spring Boot application of this module (extra main class, extra
# application.properties, a test that references them). Only api/, model/ and ApiUtil are wanted.

# Sample application, its resources and its test
**/OpenApiGeneratorApplication.java
**/OpenApiGeneratorApplicationTests.java
**/application.properties
**/application.yml
**/pom.xml
**/README.md
**/build.gradle
**/settings.gradle
**/gradlew
**/gradlew.bat
**/gradle/**

# A copy of the spec inside the jar would be a second source of truth
**/src/main/resources/openapi.yaml

# Unused with <dateLibrary>java8</dateLibrary>, and it imports Jackson 2's ISO8601DateFormat, which
# no longer exists under Spring Boot 4 (Jackson 3). Nothing references it, so drop it.
**/invoker/RFC3339DateFormat.java

# Configuration classes in the foreign package org.openapitools.configuration:
#   HomeController              -> springdoc UI redirect, needs springdoc (not a dependency here)
#   EnumConverterConfiguration  -> converter for enum path/query params, which this API has none of
# Add them back only together with their dependencies; if you do, keep them inside the
# ch.mmar.testautomation.service package so component scan actually sees them.
**/org/openapitools/configuration/HomeController.java
**/org/openapitools/configuration/EnumConverterConfiguration.java

# Generator bookkeeping
**/.openapi-generator-ignore
**/.openapi-generator/FILES
